  "id": "Compound::DB06637 - Gene::3749",
  "verbalization": "Dalfampridine is shown to interact with multiple potassium channel subunits through binding, with the specific targets Kcna6, Kcnf1, and Kcnv2 all participating in the same pathway involving Delayed Rectifier Potassium Channel Activity. This activity is ultimately linked to Kcnc4, suggesting a shared role in potassium channel function. The high scores in all three paths indicate a consistent relationship, with Dalfampridine acting as a modulator of delayed rectifier potassium channels, which are involved in cellular potassium homeostasis. The presence of multiple binding sites and the involvement of different subunits in the same functional pathway suggests that Dalfampridine may influence Kcnc4 through a common mechanism, possibly by altering channel activity or gating. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Dalfampridine exerts its effects on Kcnc4 via a pathway involving delayed rectifier potassium channels, highlighting a potential role in neuronal function or cellular electrophysiology.",
